 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Morning. We will check the blood pressure first. Please sit and keep the arm loose.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Blood pressure is one forty-eight by ninety-two, pulse seventy-eight. Oxygen saturation is ninety-eight percent. Temperature is thirty-six point eight. You may go in.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sit. Is it the cough today?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dry cough since three weeks?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): You are putting it down to a cold?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Running nose was there?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Earlier.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): Has the running nose stopped?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Breathlessness?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any wheeze?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sputum?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): You are a known hypertensive, on treatment?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Name of the tablet?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Ramipril.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dose is five milligram?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Once daily, in the morning?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Started four weeks back?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any drug allergy?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): Lungs are clear, no added sounds. Throat is not congested.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): I am thinking aloud only. This may be a leftover cold, or it may be the ramipril. I will not pin the cough to either one today. So continue the ramipril five milligram, I will give a cough syrup, and send you for a chest X-ray.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Brother.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Your brother is on lisinopril?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): He got a cough with it?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): The cough went after they changed his tablet?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (DOCTOR): Your cough started only after the ramipril?",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (DOCTOR): Alright, I am changing that plan, though I still will not call this a ramipril cough for certain. Stop the ramipril five milligram you take each morning for the hypertension, started four weeks back. Forget the cough syrup, and no X-ray today.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (DOCTOR): Start telmisartan forty milligram once every morning for the hypertension. If the cough is not better in two weeks, then we will do the chest X-ray. Come back in two weeks for the pressure check, and take the new tablet every morning.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Kindly collect the slip at the counter. I will book that two-week visit."
